	(footprint "xmitter:T50-6_Flat_HandWound"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "5fb7c3c9-d8f9-490d-b0bf-6becced81ebe")
		(at -109.775 88.925)
		(descr "T50-6 iron powder toroid (Micrometals/Amidon mix 6, yellow, A_L = 4.0 nH/N^2 = 40 microH per 100 turns-squared -- catalogs typically list the latter form; use 4.0 in the N = sqrt(L_nH / A_L) formula), hand-wound, laying flat on PCB with axis perpendicular to board. Both leads exit on the same radial side; outer lead sits just outside the OD (12.70 mm) at pad 1 (0, -7.6); inner lead sits inside the ID hole (7.70 mm) at pad 2 (0, -2.5). Pitch center-to-center 5.1 mm. Suits 9-13 turn 24 AWG magnet wire winding (e.g. 13 T for 20 m LPF nominal 676 nH). Silk shows OD and ID circles. Four 3.1 mm NPTH zip-tie holes in two tie groups: each tie has one hole just inside the ID (at X=+-2.0, Y=0) and one hole just outside the OD (at X=+-7.5, Y=0), with the tie wrapping across the donut wall on that side.  Tie direction = X axis, 90 deg from the wire-pad axis (Y).  Two ties on opposite sides of the toroid clamp it down firmly without crossing the ID center.  Hole positions: inside = +-(ID/2 - hole_radius - 0.3 mm margin) = +-2.0; outside = +-(OD/2 + 24AWG + 0.5 mm margin) = +-7.5.  Courtyard sized to cover the tie holes.")
		(tags "toroid iron powder t50-6 amidon micrometals hand wound flat ziptie")
